transport ministers are set to discuss  new rules on the maximum weights of  trucks buses and other heavy vehicles at  their council in luxembourg  the aims to improve aerodynamics fuel  efficiency and road safety  certain vehicles could have length  restrictions eased so that rear flaps  can be attached to cut down on wind drag  new cab designs will better deflect the  wind and increase safety and collisions  eu states would have six years after the  draft rules enter force to start  filtering out unfit vehicles  telecommunications ministers will take  stock of progress made on new rules to  ensure cyber security across europe  the plans to ensure a common high level  of electronic telecom security  and require all member states internet  enablers and critical infrastructure  operators to ensure a trustworthy  digital environment  discussion so far have highlighted the  need to strike a balance between  improved cyber security building the  necessary trust and making full use of  existing structures to avoid creating  new ones  the council will also focus on the  telecom single market the idea is to  create a single market for electronic  communications which will allow eu  citizens and businesses to use services  without cross-border restrictions or  heavy costs and for companies to operate  across borders regardless of where their  headquarters or clients are
 

